Last week, <em>MacRumors</em> uncovered <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/25/new-apple-tv-4k-leaked/">evidence of an Apple TV 4K (4th generation)</a>, and now an Apple support document has further hinted at a new model. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Apple-TV-Sans-Remote-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067341" /><br/>
Apple on Monday updated a <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/118295">support document</a> related to lossless audio in Apple Music with the following fine print below the Apple TV 4K section:<blockquote>Hi-Res Lossless is available only on Apple TV 4K (3rd generation or later).</blockquote>Given the Apple TV 4K (3rd generation) is the current model, the "or later" wording is noteworthy, as it could mean that a new model is imminent. However, Apple could simply be future-proofing the document or have made a mistake.<br/>
<br/>
In any case, the support document adds to growing anticipation for a new Apple TV 4K, which is expected to be announced this October.<br/>
<br/>
The next Apple TV is rumored to have an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/08/next-apple-tv-chip-leak/">A19 or A19 Pro chip</a>, an increased 8GB to 12GB of RAM, Apple Intelligence and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/19/new-apple-tv-five-rumored-upgrades/">Siri AI support</a>, an Apple-designed N1 chip with Wi-Fi 7 support, and a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/18/new-apple-tv-siri-remote-leak/">revised Siri Remote</a>. The image of the Apple TV 4K (4th generation) that we obtained last week did not reveal any design changes compared to the current model.<br/>
<br/>
